From e6f1324d97601fb228a8fc6b49ec8863a9e39a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:08:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] feat(facts): an old fact is confirmed with the owner at
 the moment of use (1690, A7)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A label is a lead, not a fact (D365), job facts go stale at about 1% a
month, and nobody fills a survey to refresh them.

- Migration 218: contact_facts gets confirmed_by_result_at,
  last_confirmed_at, confirm_asked_at; fact_confirms keeps each question.
- When a search in the owner's run shows a contact for whom the owner saved a
  core fact (occupation, employer, city, industry) older than 180 days,
  never confirmed and not asked within 180 days, the server adds ONE card
  after the reply: „შენახული მაქვს: ზურაბ — „BDO". ისევ ასეა?" with „კი,
  ასეა" / „აღარ" / „არ ვიცი" (en alike). At most one per conversation a day.
- The tap is settled by the server before any model: yes → last_confirmed_at;
  not sure → nothing more (not asked again for 180 days); no longer → „ახლა
  სად მუშაობს …?" once, and the owner's next short line is saved as a new
  fact from him — the old one is kept, never deleted.
- A „helped" debrief sets confirmed_by_result_at on the asker's core facts
  about the helper.
No model text; no settings page.

DONE WHEN: a fact saved 7 months ago gives exactly one confirm line in the
owner's chat when used; a tap updates the right field; the same fact is not
asked again; a fact younger than 180 days gives nothing; two old facts in
one conversation give one question.

